    {
      "text": "The fact that a law is enforced by a state gives it no moral weight by itself, though one may still obey it for prudential reasons.",
      "value": 2,
      "rationale": "Wolff says an anarchist may obey for prudential reasons but never regards commands as legitimate, and Simmons says illegitimacy removes any strong presumption of obedience.",
      "sources": [
        "s2",
        "s3",
